# Orca's game patches for Project+ v3.2 (launcher profile PPLUS32, on Super Smash Bros. Brawl NTSC-U
# revision 2), forced on in every Project+ session (Source/Core/Core/Orca/UX/GamePatches.h):
# `<address> <original> <value>`, hex. Applied only once the launcher has handed over to the game
# (the profile's frame hook is live), and only as guarded groups: a group is written while every
# one of its words is still the original, so nothing ever lands in Project+'s own codes or in
# another module that later occupies the memory. Never a `*` line: Project+ owns the game's data
# (the one data group below sets a default once, then leaves the words to the game).
# This file is hashed into the lobby key.

# muBootNandTask (Brawl's sora_menu_boot, loaded at 0x811A6000 on the boot scene; process
# 0x811A6300, state at +0x78), which Project+ loads unchanged at the same address (the six original
# words checked in Project+'s RAM on the save prompt, 2026-10-02). With no save in the session NAND
# (always so with Orca.app), state 5 opens Project+'s "Create save file for Project+?" and, on Yes,
# spends about 13 s writing a 14.6 MB Brawl save to the NAND before character select. In its place,
# as RSBE01.patches does for Brawl: the game's own "continue without saving" (clear the save flags,
# +0x48 &= 0xE0, and go to state 55, the end of the boot check). No dialog, no save written;
# Project+ goes on to character select by itself. A session that seeds a save never reaches state 5.
811A6430 80030068 88030048    # lbz   r0, 0x48(r3)
811A6434 83E3005C 54000634    # rlwinm r0, r0, 0, 24, 26
811A6438 2C000000 98030048    # stb   r0, 0x48(r3)
811A643C 4182001C 38000037    # li    r0, 55
811A6440 7C030378 90030078    # stw   r0, 0x78(r3)
811A6444 4AF193ED 48001204    # b     0x811A7648 (the process's end)

# The rules menu's item default, as RSBE01.patches sets it for Brawl (which describes these four
# words of Brawl's gmGlobalRecord menu data): Project+ keeps Brawl's record and its Item Switch page
# reads and writes the same words. With no save in the session NAND every match had items at
# Medium: Project+'s netplay codeset ("Default Settings Modifier") sets the stock rules but not the
# items (its tournament variants, disabled, turn them off). Instead, once, while all four words
# still hold the defaults: the frequency None, which Project+ itself takes as every item off in a
# match ("Items spoofed off if item frequency None"). The switch is left as Project+ set it (its
# GameGlobal::init hook clears the Mayhem and Passive Aggression bits, 0x00180000), so choosing a
# frequency in the rules menu brings its usual items back. The second word becomes 'ORCA' so the
# group never lands again: a player's own choice stays, Medium included. A data group, not code:
# the record is not a module, and after the boot Project+ writes these words only when a player
# leaves its Item Switch page (checked in Project+'s RAM and in its codeset's source on the SD card,
# 2026-10-02).
9017BE50 02000000 00000000    # item frequency: Medium -> None
9017BE54 00000000 4F524341    # menu data +4 (unused): 'ORCA', the group has landed
9017BE58 FFE7FFFF FFE7FFFF    # item switch: Project+'s default (guard only, left as is)
9017BE5C FFFFFFFF FFFFFFFF    # (guard only)
